.TH EXTRACT-FEMACROS 1 "2026-07-27" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
extract-femacros.py \- build the otsdaq FE macro inventory from source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tools/extract-femacros.py
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scans every
.B registerFEMacroFunction
call site in the
.B otsdaq-mu2e*
submodules and writes a machine-readable inventory of the FE macros they
register: name, handler, input and output argument names, permission level and
description, with the source file and line for each.
.PP
The call sites span many lines, are heavily interleaved with comments, and a
sizeable fraction are commented out, so the scan matches braces rather than
lines and records an
.B active
flag per registration. Registrations found in files that merely
.I generate
registration source (the tracker test-stand importer) are flagged
.B generator
and excluded from the totals.
.PP
This is a repository-maintenance tool, not an installed one. Run it after
updating the otsdaq submodules to refresh
.IR data/otsdaq-femacros.json ,
which backs the inventory in
.IR doc/otsdaq-command-surface.md .
.PP
The output is a snapshot of what the source registers. It is not the set of
macros callable on a live system: the DTC front end re-registers its child ROCs'
macros at configure time, so a running instance exposes more than appears here.
Use the otsdaq
.B getFEMacroList
request for ground truth.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-root " \fIDIR\fR"
Directory holding the
.B otsdaq-mu2e*
checkouts. Default: the
.B mu2edaq-main
parent of this checkout.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Where to write the JSON inventory. Default:
.IR data/otsdaq-femacros.json .
Use
.B \-
for standard output.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pattern " \fIGLOB\fR"
Submodule glob to scan. Default:
.BR otsdaq-mu2e* .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the summary written to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
A JSON array, one object per call site:
.PP
.RS
.nf
package, file, line   where it was found
active                false if commented out
generator             true if the file only emits registration source
name                  the macro name as callers must spell it
handler               the C++ method it dispatches to
inputs, outputs       argument names, exactly as registered
permission            requiredUserPermissions
callers               allowedCallingFEs
description           the help text, when one was given
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The root directory does not exist or holds no matching checkouts.
.SH EXAMPLES
Refresh the checked-in inventory and print the summary:
.PP
.RS
.nf
./tools/extract\-femacros.py
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect without writing anything:
.PP
.RS
.nf
./tools/extract\-femacros.py \-o \- \-q | jq '.[] | select(.active) | .name'
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data/otsdaq-femacros.json
Default output, checked in.
.TP
.I doc/otsdaq-command-surface.md
The survey this inventory supports.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-tools (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group.
